     On a different note, I was playing a wizard character for the second
or third time recently, and I noted that while not blind, he never messes
up inscribing Elbereth.  He can also attack from it for a number of rounds
before it fades, and it seems to last almost forever otherwise.
     I finally died when I was attacking from an Elbereth and it faded;
I was blinded by a floating eye (no telepathy yet) and I was cornered
by a werewolf that I didn't know existed.  "You feel hemmed in" ("You
feel like you're going to die" might have been more appropriate... without
an Elbereth, even fighting more than one wolf at a time was a bit much for
this character.)  I tried inscribing Elbereth three times (different
squares) before I died; no luck (I can see why, too).
     I'm not quite sure that on shallow levels a wizard character with
telepathy CAN be killed, unless he gets trapped on a space with a faded
"Elbereth" (or some other inscription that managed to get there), and
he can even avoid that by not fighting off of Elbereth squares.  What
kinds of monsters ignore the Elbereth besides minotaurs?  You have to
go downwards quite a ways to get there...

